        "Edit the first 2x2 layout into a clean close-up character reference sheet. Match the same four cells exactly, separated by narrow white gutters. TOP LEFT: zoomed close view of hair fastening from the exact angle of its crop, retaining the shape of the original accessory or hairstyle; TOP RIGHT: the full upper-body outfit, shoulders to waist, with garment structure legible; BOTTOM LEFT: the lower-body outfit from the waist to the shoes in frontal view; BOTTOM RIGHT: a tight detail of the fastener, stripe, garment patch or waist tie shown in the crop. Use the second image only for full-length garment proportions when the lower part was cropped. Keep colors and material, keep the grey-haired girl's original features, no captions, interface, or photographic background. Match these observations: Lily-of-the-valley flowers and a long plum ribbon on the left temple. Teal lace-edged capelet, white blouse, narrow bow and gray gloves. Overall tiered ivory skirt and gray floral band; lower edge partly obscured by the game UI. Narrow dark belt and rectangular buckle. On the upper-left tile draw the ivory-white bell flowers in neutral daylight with a dark plum ribbon. The petals are ivory-white.",
